    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "518—Washington National Airport, Washington, D. C.\n1B.H1552",
      "SCENIC ART SERIES, B. S. REYNOLDS CO., WASHINGTON, D. C.\nTHE WASHINGTON NATIONAL AIRPORT\nThe Washington National Airport, located\non Gravelly Point on the Mount Vernon Boule-\nvard between Washington and Alexandria,\nVa., is the third largest airport in the world,\nexceeded only by New York and Chicago. It\nwas built at a cost of $15,000,000 and\nopened to full time operation June 16, 1941.\nIt may be reached by taking the A. B. and\nW. bus at the terminal located in Washington\nat 10th and D Streets, N. W.\nGENUINE CURTEICH-CHICAGO 'c.T. ART-COLORTONE\" POST CARD (REG. U.S. PAT. OFF.\n150\nPLACE\nONE CENT\nSTAMP\nHERE\nPOST CARD\n2015.166.2392 QR"
